Author:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
AuthorDate: Fri May 8 10:01:20 2026 +0000
Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Fri May 8 10:01:20 2026 +0000

    Bug 671497 - Fix array desynchronization when adding threaded headers. r=mkmelin

    This patch fixes an issue where undoing a message deletion or receiving
    background mail in a threaded view corrupts the chronological sorting
    and internal view arrays.

    The root cause was that `nsMsgThreadedDBView::MoveThreadAt` and parts of
    `OnNewHeader` attempted to manually calculate index shifts and array
    insertions. This manual math was highly error-prone and frequently
    bypassed Mork's native sorting and layout logic. Furthermore, operations
    mutating the base arrays inside a locked UI state lacked proper failure
    guards, risking permanent UI freezes.

    Changes:
    * Removed the flawed and redundant `MoveThreadAt` function entirely.
    * Refactored `OnNewHeader` to use a native reconstruction strategy for
      root changes and chronological shifts: it now cleanly removes the
      stale root, relies on `nsMsgDBView::AddHdr` to determine the exact
      chronological position, and uses `ExpandByIndex` to natively rebuild
      the children from the DB.
    * Implemented `mozilla::MakeScopeExit` guards to guarantee that UI
      change notifications are unsuppressed and user selection is restored
      on any exit path (success or early return).
    * Added a new frontend Mochitest (`browser_undoInThreads.js`) to
      guarantee array stability, twisty state, and chronological sorting
      during Undo operations and background mail injection.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298696

